@@ -4,3 +4,26 @@ This file has moved. Please see the latest configuration documentation here:
 
 - Full config docs: [docs/config.md](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/docs/config.md)
 - MCP servers section: [docs/config.md#connecting-to-mcp-servers](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/docs/config.md#connecting-to-mcp-servers)
+
+## Local shell selection patch
+
+`default_shell` optionally selects the shell used for local model commands. Accepted values are
+`powershell`, `cmd`, `sh`, `bash`, and `zsh`, case-insensitively. Omit it to retain upstream shell selection.
+When set, model-provided `shell` arguments are ignored and logged at debug level.
+
+`default_shell_path` optionally supplies an absolute path to that shell's executable. With `default_shell`
+set, a missing path, relative path, or directory causes a startup error. Without a path, Codex discovers
+the selected shell type and errors if it cannot find it. A path alone does not change upstream selection.
+
+```toml
+default_shell = "sh"
+default_shell_path = "C:/Users/PC/.claude/bin/luna-sh/sh.exe"
+```
+
+Both keys also accept CLI `-c` overrides and app-server `thread/start` `config` overrides.
+Shell argv and `allow_login_shell` retain upstream semantics; use `allow_login_shell = false` if the
+selected shell should receive `-c` instead of `-lc`.
+
+Windows POSIX shells receive POSIX tool guidance. Cmd receives cmd guidance; PowerShell guidance is
+unchanged. Windows `sh` snapshots are disabled. Sandbox selection and restricted-token spawning are unchanged.
+Remote environments retain their reported native shell; configured sessions still ignore model shell requests there.
